From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 15:50:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] quickjs: Bump servo-quickjs for Intl web compatibility

servo-quickjs 879bfe9 formats dates and times as the other browsers do
where CLDR's data differs from what sites expect: plain spaces instead
of U+202F and U+2009, as SpiderMonkey does, and the date patterns of
en-CA, sv-SE and the Chinese locales its table lacked (zh-SG, zh-MO,
zh-Hans-HK, zh-Hans-MO). It also takes the system ICU's symbol suffix
from the ICU headers.

Validation: `./mach build --release --js-engine quickjs` of a tree with the same Rust code linked libicui18n.so.74, and `xvfb-run ./mach smoketest --release` passed. The 33 WPT tests that use Intl or locale APIs had the same 5 unexpected results (testdriver BiDi, web-bundle, WebRTC) as an earlier build of these shim changes; /ecmascript/locale-compat.html, which fails 4 subtests on fdb3eab, passes.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; written by the agent, which also ran the build and WPT runs above)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
---
 support/quickjs/cargo-config.toml | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/support/quickjs/cargo-config.toml b/support/quickjs/cargo-config.toml
index 357c02ca47d..45b4de1fd31 100644
--- a/support/quickjs/cargo-config.toml
+++ b/support/quickjs/cargo-config.toml
@@ -5,4 +5,4 @@
 # were tested with. The shim's version must match the mozjs version that Cargo.toml requires, or
 # Cargo leaves the patch unused.
 [patch.crates-io]
-mozjs = { git = "https://github.com/openharmony-rs/servo-quickjs", rev = "fdb3eab5a906abb563854f08eb9021d095fef18b" }
+mozjs = { git = "https://github.com/openharmony-rs/servo-quickjs", rev = "879bfe90ee0855fe9a63b7faba8c414ecdf7a37f" }
